{{ 'section-aria-header.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- if section.settings.preorder_font != blank -%}
  {% style %}
    {{ section.settings.preorder_font | font_face: font_display: 'swap' }}
    .aria-header {
      --aria-header-preorder-font: {{ section.settings.preorder_font.family }}, {{ section.settings.preorder_font.fallback_families }};
      --aria-header-preorder-weight: {{ section.settings.preorder_font.weight }};
    }
  {% endstyle %}
{%- endif -%}
{{ 'component-aria-mega-menu.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'component-aria-mobile-nav.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'aria-header.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<script src="{{ 'aria-mega-menu.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<script src="{{ 'aria-mobile-nav.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{%- liquid
  assign announcement_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'announcement'
  assign announcement_count = announcement_blocks.size
  assign show_store_links = false
  if section.settings.show_app_store or section.settings.show_google_play
    assign show_store_links = true
  endif

  comment
    There is one DEDICATED block type per parent nav item, so a panel's parent is a
    structural fact of its type rather than a label the merchant types. That is what these
    two parallel lists capture: the parent name each enabled block belongs to, and that
    block's id. The nav loop below walks them to find whether a link owns a panel.

    Deriving the label from the type is why the Theme Editor no longer asks for a parent
    label, a menu handle or any child-menu wiring.

    THE CHEVRON IS DERIVED, NOT LISTED (client change, 2026-09-08).

    There used to be a THIRD parallel list, `mega_carets`, because the approved 6337 frames
    only drew a chevron on Shop, Best Sellers and Start Here — Live showed its red dot
    instead, and Community and Dailey Deals showed nothing at all, open or closed. The
    client has since asked for the affordance to be UNIFORM: every parent that owns a
    dropdown or a mega panel shows the chevron, and nothing else does.

    That makes the chevron a FUNCTION of the nav structure rather than a per-parent design
    fact, so the list is gone and the nav loop tests `has_mega` directly — the same fact
    that wires the trigger and the drawer panel. A parent therefore cannot gain a panel
    without gaining its arrow, or keep an arrow after losing its panel.

    Do NOT reintroduce `mega_carets` from the older frame notes; section 4.6 of
    claude-context.md records this change and supersedes them.
  endcomment
  comment
    THE CHEVRON IS LISTED AGAIN (2026-09-30), reversing the 2026-09-08 note above. The
    user re-approved Figma 6316:3408, which draws the chevron on Shop, Best Sellers and
    Start Here only, and chose to follow it; `chevron_items` names those parents (every other
    parent keeps its panel, just without the arrow). Clearing the setting gives no chevrons;
    listing every parent restores the uniform rule.
  endcomment
  assign chevron_list = section.settings.chevron_items | split: ','

  comment
    MENU-ONLY PARENTS (2026-10-15, client): the parents named in `menu_only_items` (Start
    Here) only open their mega panel when clicked; they do not navigate (Start Here has no
    page of its own, and jumping to the home page's #start-here was not wanted). The link
    keeps its href for no-JS; assets/aria-mega-menu.js cancels the click and opens the
    panel. The mobile drawer drops its "View all" row for them.
  endcomment
  assign menu_only_list = section.settings.menu_only_items | split: ','

  comment
    LIVE FALLBACK (2026-09-30). Figma 6316:3408 has "Live" between Start Here and Community,
    but the nav is built from the store's Main menu, which has no Live link. Until one is
    added in admin, the desktop bar inserts it after `live_fallback_after`, with the same
    red dot, mega panel and styling as a real menu link. It stands down by itself the moment
    the menu has a link titled `live_dot_menu_item`, so there is never a second Live.
  endcomment
  assign live_label = section.settings.live_dot_menu_item | default: 'Live'
  assign inject_live = section.settings.live_fallback_enabled
  for menu_link in section.settings.main_menu.links
    if menu_link.title == live_label
      assign inject_live = false
      break
    endif
  endfor
  assign live_url = section.settings.live_fallback_url
  if live_url == blank
    assign live_url = routes.root_url | append: '/pages/live' | replace: '//', '/'
  endif

  assign mega_names = ''
  assign mega_ids = ''
  for mega in section.blocks
    assign mega_label = ''
    case mega.type
      when 'shop_mega_menu'
        assign mega_label = 'Shop'
      when 'best_sellers_mega_menu'
        assign mega_label = 'Best Sellers'
      when 'start_here_mega_menu'
        assign mega_label = 'Start Here'
      when 'live_mega_menu'
        assign mega_label = 'Live'
      when 'community_mega_menu'
        assign mega_label = 'Community'
      when 'daily_deals_mega_menu'
        assign mega_label = 'Dailey Deals'
    endcase
    if mega_label != '' and mega.settings.enabled
      assign mega_names = mega_names | append: mega_label | append: '~'
      assign mega_ids = mega_ids | append: mega.id | append: '~'
    endif
  endfor
  assign mega_name_list = mega_names | split: '~'
  assign mega_id_list = mega_ids | split: '~'

  # The mega panels' column menus (same handles as snippets/aria-mega-menu.liquid). A parent whose own URL is not the current page still gets the current-page pill when one of its column links is, e.g. Start Here on /pages/compare-shades.
  assign mega_column_handles = 'header-shop-shop-by-collection,header-shop-shop-by-color,header-start-here-wig-101-the-basics,header-start-here-guides-answers,header-live-catch-up,header-live-this-week-s-schedule,header-community-our-heart,header-dailey-deals-all-the-ways-to-save' | split: ','
-%}

<header class="aria-header color-{{ section.settings.nav_color_scheme }}">

  {%- if announcement_count > 0 or show_store_links -%}
    <div class="aria-header__announcement color-{{ section.settings.announcement_color_scheme }}">
      <div class="aria-header__announcement-inner">
        {%- if announcement_count > 0 -%}
          <div class="aria-header__announcement-track" style="--aria-announce-count: {{ announcement_count }};">
            {%- for block in announcement_blocks -%}
              <div
                class="aria-header__announcement-item"
                style="--aria-announce-index: {{ forloop.index0 }};"
                {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
              >
                {%- if block.settings.link != blank -%}
                  <a href="{{ block.settings.link }}">{{ block.settings.text }}</a>
                {%- else -%}
                  <p>{{ block.settings.text }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if show_store_links -%}
          <div class="aria-header__store-links">
            {%- comment -%}
              width/height must be the badge's real intrinsic size (V4: 76x19 and 85x19).
              They previously claimed 120x40, which collapsed the flex chain to 0px and
              left the lazy loader with nothing to observe, so the badges never loaded.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if section.settings.show_app_store -%}
              <a href="{{ section.settings.app_store_url | default: '#' }}" class="aria-header__store-link">
                <img
                  src="{{ 'app-store.png' | asset_url }}"
                  alt="App Store"
                  loading="eager"
                  width="76"
                  height="19"
                >
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if section.settings.show_google_play -%}
              <a href="{{ section.settings.google_play_url | default: '#' }}" class="aria-header__store-link">
                <img
                  src="{{ 'google-play.png' | asset_url }}"
                  alt="Google Play"
                  loading="eager"
                  width="85"
                  height="19"
                >
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="aria-header__nav-band">
    <div class="aria-header__inner aria-header__nav">
      <div class="aria-header__nav-left">
        {%- comment -%}
          The hamburger now drives the MOBILE DRAWER (`aria-mobile-nav.js`), not the old
          full-screen `.aria-header__nav-panel` overlay. It deliberately no longer carries
          `data-aria-toggle`: that is `aria-header.js`'s generic show/hide, which knows
          nothing about drawer levels, focus trapping or the body lock. `aria-controls`
          points at the drawer, which is how the drawer script finds its own trigger.

          The panel itself is kept — from 1280px up it IS the inline desktop nav — but its
          mobile overlay role is retired (see component-aria-mobile-nav.css).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="aria-header__menu-toggle"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="AriaMnav-{{ section.id }}"
        >
          {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'menu', class: 'aria-header__menu-icon-open' -%}
          {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'close', class: 'aria-header__menu-icon-close' -%}
          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.open_menu' | t }}</span>
        </button>

        <div class="aria-header__nav-panel" id="AriaNavPanel-{{ section.id }}">
          <button
            type="button"
            class="aria-header__drawer-close aria-header__nav-close"
            data-close-panel="AriaNavPanel-{{ section.id }}"
            aria-label="{{ 'aria_theme.header.close_menu' | t }}"
          >
            {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'close' -%}
          </button>
          <nav class="aria-header__primary-nav" aria-label="{{ 'aria_theme.header.primary_nav' | t }}">
            <ul class="aria-header__menu">
              {%- for link in section.settings.main_menu.links -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign is_last_item = forloop.last
                  assign highlight_item = false
                  if is_last_item and section.settings.highlight_last_item
                    assign highlight_item = true
                  endif
                  assign show_dot = false
                  if section.settings.show_live_dot and section.settings.live_dot_menu_item != blank and link.title == section.settings.live_dot_menu_item
                    assign show_dot = true
                  endif
                  assign caret_listed = false
                  for chevron_raw in chevron_list
                    assign chevron_name = chevron_raw | strip
                    if chevron_name == link.title
                      assign caret_listed = true
                      break
                    endif
                  endfor
                  assign menu_only = false
                  for menu_only_raw in menu_only_list
                    assign menu_only_name = menu_only_raw | strip
                    if menu_only_name == link.title
                      assign menu_only = true
                      break
                    endif
                  endfor
                  assign show_new = false
                  if section.settings.new_badge_text != blank and link.title == section.settings.new_badge_item
                    assign show_new = true
                  endif
                -%}
                {%- if link.links != blank -%}
                  <li class="aria-header__menu-item aria-header__menu-item--dropdown">
                    <button
                      type="button"
                      class="aria-header__menu-link aria-header__submenu-toggle{% if highlight_item %} aria-header__menu-link--highlight{% endif %}"
                      aria-expanded="false"
                    >
                      <span class="aria-header__menu-label">{{ link.title }}</span>
                      {%- if show_dot -%}
                        <span class="aria-header__live-dot aria-live-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.live_now' | t }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                      {%- comment -%}
                        SAME GLYPH AS A MEGA PARENT. This branch rendered the theme's
                        chunkier `chevron-down`, so a Shopify-submenu parent and a mega
                        parent could sit side by side in one nav with two different arrows
                        at two different stroke weights. Both now render `mega-chevron` —
                        the design file's own 14px `arrow-up-01` export — through the same
                        `.aria-header__menu-caret` class, so the size, stroke, colour, 4px
                        offset and vertical centring are shared rather than duplicated.

                        The 180-degree flip this one takes while its accordion is open
                        stays: that is a click-driven disclosure and the flip is its
                        open-state cue (`.aria-header__menu-item--dropdown.is-open`). The
                        hover-driven mega parents have the pink pill for that instead, and
                        their arrow deliberately does not move.
                      {%- endcomment -%}
                      {%- if caret_listed -%}
                        {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'mega-chevron', class: 'aria-header__menu-caret' -%}
                      {%- endif -%}
                      {%- if show_new -%}
                        <span class="aria-header__new-chip">{{ section.settings.new_badge_text }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </button>
                    <ul class="aria-header__dropdown">
                      {%- for childlink in link.links -%}
                        <li><a href="{{ childlink.url }}">{{ childlink.title }}</a></li>
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    </ul>
                  </li>
                {%- else -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign has_mega = false
                    assign mega_panel_id = ''
                    for mega_name in mega_name_list
                      if mega_name == link.title
                        assign has_mega = true
                        assign mega_panel_id = 'AriaMega-' | append: mega_id_list[forloop.index0]
                        break
                      endif
                    endfor

                    assign current_state = ''
                    if link.active
                      assign current_state = 'page'
                    else
                      assign column_prefix = 'header-' | append: link.handle | append: '-'
                      for column_handle in mega_column_handles
                        if column_handle contains column_prefix
                          for column_link in linklists[column_handle].links
                            if column_link.active
                              assign current_state = 'true'
                              break
                            endif
                          endfor
                        endif
                      endfor
                    endif
                  -%}
                  <li class="aria-header__menu-item{% if highlight_item %} aria-header__menu-item--highlight{% endif %}{% if has_mega %} aria-header__menu-item--mega{% endif %}">
                    <a
                      href="{{ link.url }}"
                      class="aria-header__menu-link{% if highlight_item %} aria-header__menu-link--highlight{% endif %}"
                      {% if has_mega %}data-aria-mega-trigger="{{ mega_panel_id }}"{% endif %}
                      {% if has_mega and menu_only %}
                        data-aria-mega-menu-only
                      {% endif %}
                      {% if current_state != '' %}
                        aria-current="{{ current_state }}"
                      {% endif %}
                    >
                      <span class="aria-header__menu-label">{{ link.title }}</span>
                      {%- if show_dot -%}
                        <span class="aria-header__live-dot aria-live-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.live_now' | t }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                      {%- comment -%}
                        A 14px `arrow-up-01` chevron 4px after the label on the parents
                        named in `chevron_items` that own a mega panel (Shop, Best Sellers
                        and Start Here per Figma 6316:3408; see the note at the top).

                        It stays visible while the panel is open: the design draws it inside
                        the open pink pill, and an earlier pass hid it there.

                        `show_dot` NO LONGER SUPPRESSES IT. The red dot and the chevron
                        answer different questions — "live right now" versus "this opens a
                        panel" — and the mobile drawer has always given Live both its dot
                        and its arrow. The dot is in flow and superscripted, so on Live the
                        chevron sits 4px after the DOT rather than 4px after the word; that
                        is the same label-then-affordance order the drawer already uses.
                      {%- endcomment -%}
                      {%- if has_mega and caret_listed -%}
                        {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'mega-chevron', class: 'aria-header__menu-caret' -%}
                      {%- endif -%}
                      {%- if show_new -%}
                        <span class="aria-header__new-chip">{{ section.settings.new_badge_text }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </a>
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if inject_live and link.title == section.settings.live_fallback_after -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign live_has_mega = false
                    assign live_panel_id = ''
                    for mega_name in mega_name_list
                      if mega_name == live_label
                        assign live_has_mega = true
                        assign live_panel_id = 'AriaMega-' | append: mega_id_list[forloop.index0]
                        break
                      endif
                    endfor
                    assign live_caret = false
                    for chevron_raw in chevron_list
                      assign chevron_name = chevron_raw | strip
                      if chevron_name == live_label
                        assign live_caret = true
                        break
                      endif
                    endfor
                  -%}
                  <li class="aria-header__menu-item{% if live_has_mega %} aria-header__menu-item--mega{% endif %}">
                    <a
                      href="{{ live_url }}"
                      class="aria-header__menu-link"
                      {% if live_has_mega %}data-aria-mega-trigger="{{ live_panel_id }}"{% endif %}
                      {% if request.path == live_url %}
                        aria-current="page"
                      {% endif %}
                    >
                      <span class="aria-header__menu-label">{{ live_label }}</span>
                      {%- if section.settings.show_live_dot -%}
                        <span class="aria-header__live-dot aria-live-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.live_now' | t }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                      {%- if live_has_mega and live_caret -%}
                        {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'mega-chevron', class: 'aria-header__menu-caret' -%}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </a>
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </nav>
        </div>

        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" class="aria-header__logo">
          {%- if section.settings.logo != blank -%}
            {{
              section.settings.logo
              | image_url: width: 400
              | image_tag:
                loading: 'eager',
                widths: '110,152,220,304',
                class: 'aria-header__logo-img',
                alt: section.settings.logo.alt | default: shop.name
            }}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              V4 shows the Wig Party wordmark at 152x40. `Logo.png` is that exact asset, so
              it ships as the built-in default — an image_picker can't be preset to a theme
              asset in JSON (it only accepts shopify:// file URLs). The shop-name text
              remains the last resort if the asset is ever removed.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <img
              src="{{ 'Logo.png' | asset_url }}"
              alt="{{ shop.name }}"
              loading="eager"
              width="152"
              height="40"
              class="aria-header__logo-img"
            >
          {%- endif -%}
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="aria-header__nav-right">
        {%- liquid
          assign use_wp_search_overlay = false
          if section.settings.wp_search_overlay and settings.predictive_search_enabled
            assign use_wp_search_overlay = true
          endif
        -%}
        {%- if use_wp_search_overlay -%}
          {%- render 'wp-search-overlay',
            placeholder: section.settings.search_placeholder,
            live_blog: section.settings.wp_search_live_blog
          -%}
          <div class="wp-search-legacy">
        {%- endif -%}
        <div class="aria-header__search">
          <button
            type="button"
            class="aria-header__search-trigger"
            data-aria-toggle
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="AriaSearchPanel-{{ section.id }}"
          >
            {%- comment -%}
              Two glyphs, same pattern as the hamburger: the trigger becomes a close control
              when its panel is open, which is what makes the compact search at 1280-1335px
              read as a toggle. Only that range swaps them (see section-aria-header.css) —
              below 1280 the panel is a full-screen overlay with its own close button, and
              from 1336 up the trigger is not rendered at all.

              The accessible name stays "Search" in both states on purpose: the button
              already carries `aria-expanded`, which is how a toggle communicates its state.
              Relabelling it as well would announce the same thing twice.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'search', class: 'aria-header__search-icon-open' -%}
            {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'close', class: 'aria-header__search-icon-close' -%}
            <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.search_label' | t }}</span>
          </button>

          <div class="aria-header__search-panel" id="AriaSearchPanel-{{ section.id }}">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="aria-header__drawer-close aria-header__search-close"
              data-close-panel="AriaSearchPanel-{{ section.id }}"
              aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}"
            >
              {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'close' -%}
            </button>
            {%- if settings.predictive_search_enabled -%}
              <predictive-search
                class="aria-header__search-form-wrap"
                data-loading-text="{{ 'accessibility.loading' | t }}"
              >
            {%- else -%}
              <search-form class="aria-header__search-form-wrap">
            {%- endif -%}

            <form action="{{ routes.search_url }}" method="get" role="search" class="aria-header__search-form">
              <input
                type="search"
                name="q"
                value="{{ search.terms | escape }}"
                placeholder="{{ section.settings.search_placeholder }}"
                class="aria-header__search-input"
                aria-label="{{ 'aria_theme.header.search_label' | t }}"
                autocomplete="off"
              >
              <input type="hidden" name="options[prefix]" value="last">
              <input type="hidden" name="type" value="product">
              <button type="reset" class="aria-header__search-reset hidden">
                {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'close' -%}
                <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.search_reset' | t }}</span>
              </button>
              <button type="submit" class="aria-header__search-submit">
                {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'search', class: 'aria-header__icon--compact' -%}
                {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'nav-search', class: 'aria-header__icon--desktop' -%}
              </button>
            </form>

            {%- if settings.predictive_search_enabled -%}
              <div class="aria-header__search-results" data-predictive-search tabindex="-1"></div>
              <span class="predictive-search-status visually-hidden" role="status" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </predictive-search>
            {%- else -%}
              </search-form>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
        {%- if use_wp_search_overlay -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Wishlist VIEW trigger. `data-wishlist-open` is the only contract — the shared
          delegated listener in assets/aria-wishlist.js opens the one drawer instance, so
          this markup can be copied anywhere (product page, collection, a future section)
          and works with no extra JS. It is a <button>, not a link: there is no wishlist
          page to fall back to, and it must never navigate.

          The count badge is `data-wishlist-count`, which the same file keeps in sync and
          hides at zero, mirroring how the cart bubble only renders for a non-empty cart.
          It starts hidden because the server cannot know a localStorage wishlist.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="aria-header__icon-btn aria-header__wishlist{% unless section.settings.show_wishlist_desktop %} aria-header__wishlist--mobile-only{% endunless %}"
          data-wishlist-open
          aria-haspopup="dialog"
          aria-label="{{ 'aria_theme.wishlist.view' | t }}"
        >
          {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'heart-outline', class: 'aria-header__icon-svg' -%}
          <span class="aria-header__cart-bubble" data-wishlist-count aria-hidden="true" hidden></span>
        </button>

        {%- if shop.customer_accounts_enabled -%}
          <shopify-account
            menu="{{ settings.customer_account_menu | default: 'customer-account-main-menu' }}"
            class="aria-header__icon-btn aria-header__account"
          >
            <span slot="signed-out-avatar" class="aria-header__icon-slot">
              {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'account', class: 'aria-header__icon--compact' -%}
              {%- render 'aria-icon', name: 'nav-user', class: 'aria-header__icon--desktop' -%}
              <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'aria_theme.header.account_label' | t }}</span>
            </span>
          </shopify-account>
        {%- endif -%}

        <a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" id="cart-icon-bubble" class="aria-header__icon-btn aria-header__cart">
          {%- render 'aria-cart-icon-bubble-content' -%}
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Panels sit here, as siblings of the nav row and direct children of the full-bleed
      `.aria-header__nav-band`, because that is the element they are positioned against.
      Nesting them inside their `<li>` would not work: `.aria-header__menu-item` is
      `position: relative` from 1280px up, so each panel would be trapped in a
      ~100px-wide containing block instead of spanning the viewport.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- for mega in section.blocks -%}
      {%- unless mega.type == 'announcement' -%}
        {%- if mega.settings.enabled -%}
          {%- capture mega_id -%}AriaMega-{{ mega.id }}{%- endcapture -%}
          {%- render 'aria-mega-menu',
            block: mega,
            id: mega_id,
            ticker: section.settings.mega_ticker_text
          -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    MOBILE DRAWER (below 1280px). Rendered outside `.aria-header__nav-band` because it is a
    viewport-level `position: fixed` dialog, not part of the nav row, and it must stack above
    the band's own panels rather than inside them.

    It is handed the SAME two parallel lists the desktop nav loop uses, so a parent gets a
    drawer panel on exactly the condition it gets a mega panel — no second source of truth
    for which items have children.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'aria-mobile-nav',
    section: section,
    menu: section.settings.main_menu,
    mega_names: mega_names,
    mega_ids: mega_ids
  -%}
</header>

